/target
**/*.rs.bk
Cargo.lock

# Workflow plan artifacts written by `smart-coder plan` (spec 09) — run output,
# not source.
.smart-coder/

# Workflow ownership leases (spec 19). Unlike the artifacts beside them in
# specs/<slug>/, a lease is *runtime* state — who is writing this directory right
# now — and is meaningless in another checkout. Committing one would also make a
# dead process look like a live holder to whoever cloned it.
lease.json

# Stray stdout/stderr redirect logs from launching the GUI during dev.
sc-win-launch-*.log
.dc/

# Tailscale TLS cert/key (local, never commit)
*.ts.net.crt
*.ts.net.key

# Rust->Android native build output (regenerable from crates/sc-android)
**/jniLibs/**/*.so

# Local secrets: API keys (Gemini, etc.) loaded at startup by sc_model::load_dotenv. NEVER commit.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Personal Claude Code tooling — local to a contributor's machine, not project source.
.claude/

# The browser interface is built by Vite and embedded with `include_str!`.
# **Generated, so not committed** — CI installs Node and builds it, which is the
# trade recorded in spec 18: a checked-in bundle is one somebody forgets to
# rebuild, and a stale one ships silently with every test still green.
crates/sc-server/assets/ui/
node_modules/
web/test-results/
web/playwright-report/
# TypeScript's incremental-build caches. Machine-local timestamps and file
# hashes, rewritten by every `tsc` run — committing them means a diff on every
# build that says nothing about the source, and a merge conflict in a file
# nobody can usefully resolve.
*.tsbuildinfo
